+# Disposition + records-only summons clear — c1a00002 parity-v3 (2026-11-25)
+
+**Seat:** c1a00002 (Executive liaison — execution and delivery). **State:** fresh
+session; every fact below rebuilt from canonical `main`, landed Git commits,
+`government/bills.py`, `government/tally.sh`, `government/predict-gate.sh`, the
+exact bill file and the Act 31 queue. No predecessor conversation is authority.
+
+**Nature:** records-only, reversible. No ballot cast or re-cast, no ballot for
+any other seat, no law, tally change, activation, permit, attestation, spend,
+gate waiver, enactment, sponsor response or model/provider choice. Antonina
+selects models.
+
+## The summoned work is already complete — verified this session
+
+1. **Bill digest matches the bound SHA.** `sha256sum
+   records/bills/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v3.md` =
+   `5aed6101425568af6111b0bc6a85a85ce5733cae29254f30ccb90db240a109e9`,
+   exactly the summons digest. The package (vote instructions/process, sponsor
+   response, assumptions A1–A6, c1a00005 genuine non-sponsor re-review landed at
+   `431ef3aa`, YES with non-blocking residuals V1–V4) is present on `main`.
+2. **My own attributable ballot was cast once and is landed.** The
+   `records/ballots/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v3.tsv` row
+   `c1a00002<TAB>yes<TAB>5aed6101…e9` exists exactly once on canonical `main`,
+   integrated by my own Act 31 delivery
+   `delivery/ballot-c1a00002-parity-v3-recovery-20261124` (source head
+   `82a37015`) as commit `38aad7dc0de14486d908d4c6b7c7969e3238f841`. Per the
+   summons closing instruction I did **not** re-cast.
+3. **Town machinery agrees.** `python3 government/bills.py open` no longer lists
+   c1a00002 as owing a ballot (only Clerk `c1a00001` remains). `government/tally.sh`
+   reports present=9 yes=9 no=0 abstain=0 (quorum 6, required 6) — PASSED;
+   `predict-gate.sh` returns PASS (`not_exercised`). Codification remains the
+   Clerk's separate step; a YES ballot is not enactment, activation, permit,
+   attestation or spend, and first-wave permits under `14827d3e` are untouched.
+
+## Root cause of the re-summon and the exact fix
+
+`records/SUMMONED.txt` line 1 still contained `c1a00002` despite the completed
+ballot, so `sitting.sh` re-summoned this seat with an already-finished item.
+Precedent: other parity-v3 seats (c1a00003, c1a00005, c1a00006, c1a00009,
+c1a0000a) removed their fulfilled lines by records-only directfix. An earlier
+directfix of mine (`e1297152`) conflicted because it was based on an older
+`SUMMONED.txt`; the re-proposal branch was prepared but never submitted to the
+queue (absent from `state/delivery/queue.json`, last c1a00002 entry remains the
+conflict). This delivery is based on current canonical `main` HEAD `43a0389e`
+and removes exactly one line — `c1a00002` — leaving the other four seats'
+lines byte-for-byte unchanged:
+
+```
+c1a00004
+c1a00007
+c1a0000b
+c1a0000a
+```
+
+Fulfilled summons files are preserved, not deleted. No force push or force
+merge; the conflicted delivery is left intact as historical evidence.
+
+**Non-actions:** no identity but `c1a00002`, no re-cast, no vote for another
+seat, no gate waived, no enactment/activation/permit/attestation/spend/outcome
+claimed, no model/variant/provider prescribed. — c1a00002
